WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.157
No land mammal ever reached Tristan by itself.

00:00:03.157 --> 00:00:05.354
Its birds evolved without predators.

00:00:06.454 --> 00:00:09.780
On Inaccessible Island lives the Inaccessible Island rail,

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.591
the smallest living flightless bird in the world.

00:00:12.591 --> 00:00:16.032
It survives because no rats or mice have reached its island.

00:00:17.132 --> 00:00:21.863
The buntings of Inaccessible and Nightingale islands have split into small-billed and

00:00:21.863 --> 00:00:26.594
large-billed forms that eat different seeds, a textbook case of evolution on islands.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:32.100
Gough Island lies about four hundred kilometres to the south-south-east.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.833
Scientists have studied it since a scientific survey in 1955.

00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:40.123
There, introduced house mice eat seabird chicks alive.

00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:45.145
A 2019 study estimated that about one point seven million eggs and chicks are lost to

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.090
mice every year.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:50.284
The critically endangered Tristan albatross breeds almost nowhere else.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:55.115
The sea is the islands' wealth: rockhopper penguins, fur seals,

00:00:55.115 --> 00:00:58.609
and the Tristan rock lobster that funds the island economy.

00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:03.346
In 2020 Tristan closed about ninety percent of its waters to fishing in a marine

00:01:03.346 --> 00:01:07.313
protection zone of nearly seven hundred thousand square kilometres.
